**/.terraform/

# Lock files stay ignored for the control-plane / category stacks, which a human applies from a
# workstation and where a stale pin is a nuisance rather than a hazard.
#
# The five PROJECT templates are the exception and are tracked. They are what the runner provisions
# customer infrastructure from, and leaving them unpinned meant every `tofu init` resolved live: the
# e2e nightly died at 47s on a registry 500 (2026-07-27), and — quieter — it resolved a different
# provider set than the runner image had baked, so the run meant to prove production works exercised
# another dependency graph (#1259). Enforced by `pnpm -C apps/console run check:tofu-lockfiles`.
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
!templates/project/*/.terraform.lock.hcl
**/terraform.tfvars
**/backends/
**/variable-template/

# Override files are a LOCAL escape hatch and must never be tracked. OpenTofu merges `*_override.tf`
# on top of the stack's own config, so a committed one silently re-points every operator — which is
# exactly how `infra/azure-e2e` spent months on a `backend "local" {}` nobody meant to keep (#1887).
# If you need an override, it is yours alone; the fix belongs in the stack.
**/*_override.tf
**/override.tf
